385 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (In early February 2025, astronomers at the Thuringian State Observatory observed significant spectral changes in the recurrent nova T Coronae Borealis \(T CrB\). Over a two-week period, emission lines in the spectrum intensified sharply, indicating a substantial increase in the accretion rate. Additionally, new emission lines corresponding to temperatures of at least 40,000 K have emerged, potentially signaling an impending nova eruption. Despite these spectral changes, the system's brightness has remained constant. Continuous monitoring is underway to detect any forthcoming outburst. )
/E (In early February 2025, astronomers at the Thuringian State Observatory observed significant spectral changes in the recurrent nova T Coronae Borealis \(T CrB\). Over a two-week period, emission lines in the spectrum intensified sharply, indicating a substantial increase in the accretion rate. Additionally, new emission lines corresponding to temperatures of at least 40,000 K have emerged, potentially signaling an impending nova eruption. Despite these spectral changes, the system's brightness has remained constant. Continuous monitoring is underway to detect any forthcoming outburst. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
