/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (  Messier 76 in Perseus: For a challenge, spot the Little Dumbbell Nebula, a planetary nebula between the Perseus and Cassiopeia constellations. With an apparent magnitude of 12.0, you will need a large telescope and dark skies. You can find both M76 and the famous Andromeda Galaxy \(M31\) one hour after sunset, but only for a limited time, as these objects disappear after April. They will reappear in the late-night sky by September. )
/E (  Messier 76 in Perseus: For a challenge, spot the Little Dumbbell Nebula, a planetary nebula between the Perseus and Cassiopeia constellations. With an apparent magnitude of 12.0, you will need a large telescope and dark skies. You can find both M76 and the famous Andromeda Galaxy \(M31\) one hour after sunset, but only for a limited time, as these objects disappear after April. They will reappear in the late-night sky by September. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
